  <issue>
  API tests don't test permissions
### What I'm trying to achieve
Tests suite should be precise. Now all non-user actions are tested using `admin_api_client` fixture which operates on superuser privileges level. This way, we don't test if staff API endpoints contain correct permissions checking.
In the future, it may lead to a potential security issue.

### What I expected to happen
Staff API endpoints tests should use `staff_api_client` fixture and add correct permissions at the beginning of the test. Insufficient permissions test case should be covered as well.


Refactor API client in tests
Calling API in tests requires us to write some repetitive code:
```
admin_api_client.post(reverse('api'), {'query': query, 'variables': variables})
```

Both the URL and structure of the data dictionary are the same in every API, so we could adjust the `post` method of our `ApiClient` and have something like:
```
admin_api_client.post(query, variables)
```

We could also experiment with passing permissions to be used for a particular call, e.g.
```
admin_api_client.post(query, variables, permissions=[permission_manage_orders])
```

